1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,180
In my memory, winters always used to be really unpleasant.
在我的记忆中，冬天总是非常令人不快。

2
00:00:05,180 --> 00:00:09,410
You had to bundle up just to keep warm when you went outside.
你出门的时候不得不裹得严严实实（bundle up）来保暖。

3
00:00:09,410 --> 00:00:16,720
You were often cold, wet and never more than a sodden misstep away from a patch of black ice.
你常常又冷又湿，而且只要一不小心踩在湿漉漉的地方，就可能滑倒在一块黑冰上。

4
00:00:16,720 --> 00:00:22,500
If you didn't have a nasty slide, you'd arrive home to an ice-cold house.
如果你没有重重地滑一跤，回到家也会发现房子冷冰冰的。

5
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:25,730
And that would mean turning on the heating and waiting.
那就意味着要打开暖气然后等着。

6
00:00:25,730 --> 00:00:29,380
It's a miracle you didn't get chilled to the bone.
你没有被冻透（chilled to the bone）就是个奇迹了。

7
00:00:29,380 --> 00:00:33,970
Fortunately, things don't have to be so challenging any more.
幸运的是，事情不必再如此具有挑战性了。

8
00:00:33,970 --> 00:00:40,540
Technology, engineering and design have advanced giving us new solutions to old problems.
科技、工程和设计都取得了进步，为我们解决老问题提供了新的办法。

9
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:45,660
It means dealing with winter needn't be like skating on thin ice.
这意味着应对冬天不必再如履薄冰。

10
00:00:45,660 --> 00:00:51,470
With a smart thermostat, our homes can be toasty when we need them to be.
有了智能恒温器（smart thermostat），我们的家可以在我们需要的时候变得温暖舒适（toasty）。

11
00:00:51,470 --> 00:01:00,310
Many models feature smartphone apps that allow you to regulate temperature remotely, so we can warm up the house before we arrive home.
许多型号都有智能手机应用程序，让你可以远程调节（regulate）温度，这样我们就可以在到家之前就把房子预热起来。

12
00:01:00,310 --> 00:01:16,100
According to techradar.com, the largest UK-based consumer technology news and reviews website, Tado's model features voice control, while the Nest 'learns' your habits and automatically heats the home for you.
据英国最大的消费科技新闻和评论网站techradar.com报道，Tado的型号具有语音控制功能，而Nest则能“了解”你的习惯并自动为你家供暖。

13
00:01:16,100 --> 00:01:19,620
Clothes have been given an upgrade, too.
衣服也得到了升级。

14
00:01:19,620 --> 00:01:25,130
Electronic thermal jackets, hoodies and parkas heat up when you turn them on.
电子保暖夹克、连帽衫和派克大衣一打开就会升温。

15
00:01:25,130 --> 00:01:28,600
What better way to keep snug in the dead of winter?
在隆冬时节，还有什么更好的保持温暖舒适（snug）的方法呢？

16
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:36,340
At the touch of a button, or through an app on our phones, the clothing generates heat from elements placed inside.
只需按下一个按钮，或者通过我们手机上的应用程序，这些衣服内置的元件就会产生热量。

17
00:01:36,340 --> 00:01:42,980
Many models offer three levels of heating which stay warm for over 12 hours.
许多款式都提供三个加热档位，能持续保暖超过12个小时。

18
00:01:42,980 --> 00:01:46,470
Finally, there is the headgear.
最后，还有头部装备（headgear）。

19
00:01:46,470 --> 00:01:58,320
Beanies and earmuffs that feature speakers included in the fabric using Bluetooth technology so we can listen to our favourite music or, in some cases, have a phone call using the in-built microphone.
针织帽和耳罩织物中内置了使用蓝牙技术的扬声器，这样我们就可以听自己喜欢的音乐，在某些情况下，还可以使用内置麦克风打电话。

20
00:01:58,320 --> 00:02:02,660
All while keeping the head warm and avoiding a chill.
所有这些都可以在保持头部温暖避免受寒的同时完成。

21
00:02:02,660 --> 00:02:08,310
For many, the thought of winter used to be enough to make their blood run cold.
对许多人来说，过去一想到冬天就足以让他们不寒而栗。

22
00:02:08,310 --> 00:02:12,020
But using technology, life needn't freeze up.
但借助科技，生活不必停滞不前。

23
00:02:12,020 --> 00:02:18,840
With the right solutions, there's no reason why winter can't be really, really cool.
有了合适的解决办法，冬天完全有理由变得非常美好。
